# =============================================================================
# Trivy ignore list — accepted base-image vulnerabilities
# =============================================================================
# The relay and ui images share the python:3.12-slim-trixie (Debian 13) base.
# List here only CRITICAL CVEs that have NO fixed Debian version available, so
# they cannot be resolved by patching, `apt-get upgrade`, or rebasing onto a
# newer base-image digest. Each one is accepted as documented risk — see the
# "Known Accepted Risks" section in SECURITY.md for the full rationale.
#
# This file is auto-loaded by Trivy from the repository root, so a scan
# configured to fail on CRITICAL findings passes with the acceptance recorded
# in version control. Re-review when Debian ships fixes and drop resolved entries.
#
# Last reviewed: 2026-11-26
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# No accepted CVEs at the moment: the move to Debian 13 cleared the four
# entries that were listed for Debian 12 (CVE-2023-45853 zlib, CVE-2026-8376
# and CVE-2026-42496 perl-base, CVE-2025-7458 libsqlite3), and Trivy reports
# no CRITICAL findings for the current images.
